<section class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">What it will hear</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    Bravo will listen to 1090&nbsp;MHz all the time and decode the ADS-B
    position messages, Extended Squitter (DF17).
  </p>
  <div class="columns">
    <div>
      <h3>It will receive.</h3>
      <p>Airliners, business jets, helicopters and the touring aircraft whose transponder has ADS-B out.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>It will not receive.</h3>
      <p>A transponder without ADS-B out, UAT, TIS-B or ADS-R. Nor ADS-L or FLARM, which the Go receives.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">Bravo with your phone</h2>
  <div class="columns">
    <div>
      <h3>In your app.</h3>
      <p>It will send the traffic over Bluetooth in the same format as a Go, for SkyDemon, SDVFR and the other apps that read it.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>An alarm you feel.</h3>
      <p>Its buzzer and vibration motor will warn you of ADS-B traffic closing in.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Not a transmitter.</h3>
      <p>It will not broadcast your position. To be seen in ADS-L, add a Go.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">Bravo with a Go</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    Paired with a Go, Bravo will pass the ADS-B traffic to it, and the Go will
    show ADS-B, ADS-L and FLARM on one radar. The Go keeps broadcasting your
    position in ADS-L. Together they make a skyBlip Tango.
  </p>
  <p class="more"><%= link_to_page "skyblip-tango", label: "What a Tango will do" %></p>
</section>

<section id="status" class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">Where it stands</h2>
  <div class="columns">
    <div>
      <h3>The hardware.</h3>
      <p>On sale at Seeed Studio. It ships with Meshtastic, a messaging firmware that receives no ADS-B.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>The firmware.</h3>
      <p>In development, open source. You will install it on your X1 when it is released.</p>
      <p class="note"><a href="https://github.com/fcatuhe/skyblip/issues/184">Follow it on GitHub</a></p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>The tests.</h3>
      <p>The X1 has not yet been tested with skyBlip. Reception, range and altitude handling remain unverified.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

