<section class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">Your questions, answered</h2>
  <div class="faq">
    <details>
      <summary>Does Bravo make me visible?</summary>
      <p>No. Bravo will not transmit your position. To be seen in ADS-L, you need a Go, alone or paired with your Bravo as a Tango.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I use the X1 before the skyBlip firmware is released?</summary>
      <p>With Meshtastic only, which receives no ADS-B. Bravo needs the skyBlip firmware. Its install steps will be on this page when it is released.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>My aircraft has a transponder. Will its own signal show as traffic?</summary>
      <p>It will not, once you set your aircraft&rsquo;s ICAO address, on Bravo or on the Go it is paired with. Bravo will then leave your own transponder out.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need a Go?</summary>
      <p>No. Alone, Bravo will feed your navigation app. With a Go, you will also get the ADS-L and FLARM traffic, and the Go broadcasts your position in ADS-L.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need a ground station?</summary>
      <p>No. Bravo will receive ADS-B in the aircraft, wherever the signal reaches it.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
